From 5f7dce040f0e626c180e0cf191982c7793c34fe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 01:09:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Fix runData: FD version range, recipe book tabs,
 undefined tags, cross-mod assets

- neoforge.mods.toml: fix farmersdelight dependency versionRange from
  "[1.21.1-1.3.0,)" to "[1.3.0,)" -- FD's own mods.toml declares its version
  as plain "1.3.4" (the "1.21.1-" prefix is only a Modrinth/Maven artifact
  convention), so the old range made every real FD version compare as too low
  and fail mod loading entirely.
- Add the required .setRecipeBookTab(...) call to all 23
  CookingPotRecipeBuilder recipes (16 were still missing it). FD's real
  1.21.1 CookingPotRecipe codec encodes this field via
  optionalFieldOf("recipe_book_tab", MISC), and DFU's default-comparison
  helper does Optional.of(null) when the builder's tab field is left at its
  null default, hard-crashing recipe serialization for every one of these
  recipes (including matcha_latte, ender_nectar, and the milkshake/soup/stew
  recipes) via a bare NPE.
- Populate CommonTags.Items.FOODS_RAW_CHICKEN/BEEF/PORK/MUTTON and their
  COOKED_ variants with the obvious vanilla item: FD declares these tag
  constants but ships no json for them, so referencing them via .addTag(...)
  in the umbrella FOODS_MEAT_RAW/COOKED tags failed NeoForge's tag-graph
  validation ("missing following references").
- Work around this project's ExistingFileHelper not scanning dependency mod
  jars (only src/main/resources and our own generated output are visible to
  it) for two real, cross-mod asset references that exist fine at runtime but
  fail existence checks at datagen time: FD's template_pie models (now
  referenced via ModelFile.UncheckedModelFile instead of withExistingParent)
  and FD's crate_bottom texture plus Undergarden's gloomgourd_side/top
  textures (now pre-registered via existingFileHelper.trackGenerated).

runData now completes cleanly: Loot Tables, Recipes, Block/Item/Entity Tags,
Block States, Item Models, and Languages all finish without error. Includes
the regenerated src/generated/resources output (also picks up the 1.21
datapack folder rename: tags/items -> tags/item, advancements -> advancement,
recipes -> recipe, loot_tables -> loot_table).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
